  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Randy V\u00e1squez bought them four good innings, the lineup cashed it early, and this one never felt close.",
    "what_this_means": "They led from the first inning onward. Four runs in the opening frame set the tone and Jackson Merrill's two-run shot in the fifth made it a rout. Samad Taylor went 3-for-5 with a homer and three RBI, the kind of night where one player doesn't carry the load so much as confirm it. The offense showed up. They didn't need to fight for this one. The bullpen held after V\u00e1squez exited. Matsui struck out two in the sixth, and the back end sealed it without drama. This is what nine runs on ten hits looks like: decisive, clean, decided before the seventh inning arrived. They were never trailing, never in trouble, never made it close. It worked because the early swing was enough.",
    "what_to_watch": "Trevor Rogers is starting for Baltimore tonight at 10:35 AM PT, and his 6.15 ERA is the kind of number that invites the bats to show up early. Walker Buehler has been sharp lately. 3.10 in his last four. Which means this is a matchup where both teams could break it open fast.",
